.TH QWHOST 1 "March 2026" "Local-LLM-Unsensored" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qwhost \- Tor Onion Service Host & Key Persistence Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qwhost start
.I <port>
.RI [name]
.br
.B qwhost stop
.RI [name]
.br
.B qwhost list
.br
.B qwhost backup
.RI [--dest\ path]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qwhost
manages local Tor Onion v3 services mapped to local TCP ports (such as web servers, APIs, or CLL UI).
It guarantees that your .onion address remains permanent and immutable across computer reboots by persisting Ed25519-V3 private keys in ~/.local/share/qwen/onion_services/ with strict 0600 permissions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI start " <port> [name]"
Exposes local port to Tor as a persistent Onion v3 service. If [name] already exists, restores the exact same .onion URL.
.TP
.BI stop " [name]"
Tears down active Onion service in the Tor daemon without deleting the private key.
.TP
.B list
Displays all configured and active Onion services, target ports, and .onion hostnames.
.TP
.B backup
Creates an encrypted/chmod-600 tarball archive of all onion service private keys.
.SH SECURITY
Never share or expose *.key files. The .onion address is derived directly from the private key.
.SH AUTHORS
